      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe server warmup sends a text request instead of an image request whenever encoder SWA bounded replay is enabled, because replay used to reject images. #45048 serves image requests under replay on CUDA, so a VLM served with replay starts without warming its image path.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- The warmup choice moves into `_warmup_with_image`.\n- Under encoder SWA bounded replay, the non-disaggregated warmup now sends the image request on CUDA. Off CUDA, where replay still rejects images (`tokenizer_manager.py`), it keeps the text request. PD warmup is unchanged and sends text.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable: startup warmup only.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Validation\n\nA new `TestWarmupWithImage` in `test_http_server_warmup.py` covers replay on and off CUDA, without replay, and a model without image understanding. It fails before the change (partly because `http_server` did not import `get_platform`) and passes after.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\nDeveloped with AI assistance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39288452999](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39288452999)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39288453009](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39288453009)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39288453125](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39288453125)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n\n",
